    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5145" root="جحفل" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَحْفَلٌ</span></b>  <i>An army:</i> (S:) or <i>a numerous army.</i>
(K.) MF holds it to be formed, with an augmentative <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ل</span>, from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الجَحْفُ</span>, meaning “ the taking, ”
or “ carrying, ” a thing “ away. ” (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  A <i>great</i>
man: (K:) or a man <i>of great estimation</i> or
<i>dignity.</i> (S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>A generous, noble,</i> or <i>high-born,
chief</i> or <i>lord.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <i>Great in the sides.</i>
(IAar, K.)

